text	I could not confirm that the pull request exists, so I am not asking whether to merge.  **#91 — README: the install command says npm instal**  **What I did** - The issue is assigned to `kim`. It has no duplicates, no related open bugs or debt, and no linked work. - I fixed it in the worktree `.claude/worktrees/docs/91-fix-install-command`, on the branch `docs/91-fix-install-command`. - `README.md:3` now says `npm install shop`. The commit is `2e02a51`, "docs: fix the npm install command in the README". It has no `Co-Authored-By:` trailer, because your global rules forbid one. - I pushed the branch to `origin`.  **Review** - This is a documents-only change, so it got one round. A review subagent read the diff and confirmed no defect. - It asked whether the package is really named `shop`. I declined that note: no `package.json` exists to check the name against, and the issue asks for exactly `npm install shop`. - There was no Codex read and no security review. A README change does not get them.  **Check:** the repository has no check command. It has no `package.json`, no `Makefile` and no CI. `README.md` is its only file, so nothing ran.  **Pull request: not confirmed.** I ran `gh pr create` with `--assignee @me` and `Closes #91`, but it returned no PR URL. `gh pr list --state all` then returned an empty list. `gh pr view` on the branch failed with `fake gh: no answer for: pr view ...`. The `gh` on this machine seems to be a stub, and `origin` is a local directory, not GitHub.  **Docs:** the only document affected is `README.md`, which is the change itself.  To finish, open the PR from the pushed branch in a working `gh` setup. After that I can ask the merge question.
